Package: annotatR
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Layer Region-of-Interest Annotation for Images and Spectral Cubes
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@charite.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Annotate multiple layers of regions of interest across whole-slide
    microscopy images, hyperspectral data cubes, and conventional rasters.
    Annotations are stored as validated simple-feature geometries in image pixel
    coordinates with explicit pyramid-level transforms, and can be rasterised to
    binary, labelled, or multi-class integer masks for downstream segmentation and
    classification workflows. A batch annotation application built on 'shiny' and
    'OpenSeadragon' supports resumable sessions across image queues, live mask
    preview, and export to 'GeoJSON', 'QuPath', and 'TIFF' formats.
